name: Telecom re-rating (tariff validation)
tagline: "Independent re-rating of rated usage against an effective-dated tariff - tariff-table hygiene, ambiguity verdicts and an unbilled preview, over a synthetic corpus"
description: "A re-rating / tariff-validation content pack (slices R0 to R2 of the plan: tariff versioning, ambiguity, causes and root causes). Two feeds - the rated usage a billing system produced, and the tariff as one row per version with its own effective dates and an optional PRIORITY - and four chained sql.template Jobs. rr_tariff_hygiene judges the tariff table itself (rows in force at once with the same rate or different rates, gaps, negative or missing rates, inverted intervals) and rr_rerate re-rates each call at its start, giving one verdict per call (single, agree, precedence, disagree, none), an expected charge or an expected RANGE, and separate under-charged and over-billed amounts that never net. A call that an ambiguous tariff could justify is explained, not leakage. rr_explain then tests each leakage or over-billing against counterfactual re-rating (a stale version, a lower-priority row, a version billed early), with a confidence that is exactness times support and every other fitting cause kept, and rr_root_cause groups the findings into root causes with revenue at risk (never including over-billing), a run rate and two KPIs. It compares nothing with the invoice and raises no Alert: those arrive in the next slices. Every threshold is configuration. This pack is an unbilled preview: it is not priced or ordered yet. Needs the Standard, Advanced or Preview edition."
minEdition: standard
icon: heroicons_outline:calculator
contents[7]: "2 Pipelines + schemas (rated usage, tariff versions)", "4 chained sql.template Jobs (tariff hygiene, re-rating, explanation, root causes)", "6 Datasets (2 feeds, 4 Job-written)", "2 KPIs (revenue at risk, over-billed amount)", "Zero-row schema seeds", "Runbook skeleton", "Example SLA policies and Escalation Rules (inert)"
